{"name":"Blue Mosque","hex":"#21426b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"mosque","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place of worship for Muslims, often having at least one minaret; a masjid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mosque"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Mosque, Istanbul","blocks":[{"text":"The Sultan Ahmed Mosque, popularly known as the Blue Mosque, is an Ottoman-era historical imperial mosque located in Istanbul, Turkey. It was constructed between 1609 and 1617 during the rule of Ahmed I. It attracts a large number of tourists and is one of the most iconic and popular monuments of Ottoman architecture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Istanbul_%2834223582516%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Istanbul_%2834223582516%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Mosque%2C_Istanbul","wikidata":"Q80541"},{"title":"Blue Mosque, Tabriz","blocks":[{"text":"The Blue Mosque, also known as the Masjed-e Moẓaffariya and as the Kabood Mosque, is a former mosque and mausoleum complex, in a partial ruinous state, partially preserved as a museum, located in Tabriz, East Azerbaijan province, Iran. The construction of the former mosque started during the Qarā Qoyunlu dynasty and was completed in 1465, but the mausoleum extension south of the mosque was completed later during the reign of the Āq Qoyunlu, into the 1480s CE."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Blue_Mosque_%28Tabriz%29_General_view.jpg/330px-Blue_Mosque_%28Tabriz%29_General_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Mosque%2C_Tabriz","wikidata":"Q1519733"},{"title":"Mosque","blocks":[{"text":"A mosque, also called a masjid, is a place of worship for Muslims. The term usually refers to a covered building, but can be any place where Islamic prayers are performed, such as an outdoor courtyard."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Masjid_e_Nabawi_Interior_2.jpg/330px-Masjid_e_Nabawi_Interior_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mosque","wikidata":"Q32815"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Portrait_of_Sultan_Ahmed_I.png/500px-Portrait_of_Sultan_Ahmed_I.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Portrait_of_Sultan_Ahmed_I.png/500px-Portrait_of_Sultan_Ahmed_I.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Contemporary portrait of Sultan Ahmed I, who ordered the construction of the Blue Mosque. Metropolitan Museum of Art.[3]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APortrait_of_Sultan_Ahmed_I.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Relation_nouvelle_d%27un_voyage_de_Constantinople_-_enrichie_de_plans_levez_par_l%27auteur_sur_les_lieux%2C_and_des_figures_de_tout_ce_qu%27il_y_a_de_plus_remarquable_dans_cette_ville_%281680%29_%2814586728998%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Relation_nouvelle_d%27un_voyage_de_Constantinople_-_enrichie_de_plans_levez_par_l%27auteur_sur_les_lieux%2C_and_des_figures_de_tout_ce_qu%27il_y_a_de_plus_remarquable_dans_cette_ville_%281680%29_%2814586728998%29.jpg/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Relation_nouvelle_d%27un_voyage_de_Constantinople_-_enrichie_de_plans_levez_par_l%27auteur_sur_les_lieux%2C_and_des_figures_de_tout_ce_qu%27il_y_a_de_plus_remarquable_dans_cette_ville_%281680%29_%2814586728998%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"17th-century illustration with floor plan by French explorer Guillaume-Joseph Grelot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARelation_nouvelle_d'un_voyage_de_Constantinople_-_enrichie_de_plans_levez_par_l'auteur_sur_les_lieux%2C_and_des_figures_de_tout_ce_qu'il_y_a_de_plus_remarquable_dans_cette_ville_(1680)_(14586728998).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Interieur_de_la_Mosqu%C3%A9e_Ahmed_-_DPLA_-_ea640e6a581430dd574fbb4922e8bcdd.jpg/500px-Interieur_de_la_Mosqu%C3%A9e_Ahmed_-_DPLA_-_ea640e6a58143